mod:receiver_too_deep;
// A RECEIVER TOO DEEP TO READ IS NO PLACE TO TAKE (DEF-430's receiver road, landing 177d2b4). A method whose receiver is a pointer takes its
// receiver's address, as `@` does. Every question the typer asks of that place (`fixed`, through a slice, limited, lent, a view, frozen, sealed)
// walks it with a fuel of 64 and answers "nothing to refuse" at its end, and the escape walk's root answers none there, so a receiver 64 or more
// field and index steps deep (each `.f`, `[i]` or `[lo...hi]`; a `<-` ends the count) was taken unasked: a `fixed` module binding's part written
// (`rv_65`: read-only memory, 97 at -O0), a limited field left its rule (`lr_65`: 80), a by-value parameter's string freed under its caller
// (`ln_65`: 83, 97 under the freed-heap detector), a holder declared outside the block kept the receiver's address past it (`rv_k64`, DEF-622's
// store face at 64 steps: 236, 97 under the detector), and a `fixed` local's part written through a `dyn` method (`dyl_64`: 69). The explicit
// `@` of the same place is TYPE-024 already (`require_place_operand`); the receiver road now asks `place_root`'s walk once, before its
// questions, and refuses the same way. Each module is one cell; a cell's `main` stands here as `cell_main_<cell>`. 63 steps keep their own
// codes (TYPE-071, TYPE-063, TYPE-085, BORROW-002); the right programs at 63 steps and split at a pointer are `receiver_too_deep_ok.npk`.
// 2026-11-08, landing 177d2b4 (DEF-430, row 2; management_30's ruling of 01:37): the typer now refuses a place 64 or more storage steps from its root
// where it types it (Part A: each `.f`, `[i]`, `[lo...hi]` and `<-` counted, TYPE-024), so each receiver here is refused at its own span, two columns
// left of the call's, and the call passes 0 before the receiver road asks anything: row 1's check there, unreachable now, is gone. The cells' other
// reads of a place 64 or more storage steps deep are refused the same way: ten sites, the five receivers' and five reads'.
error:E5;
func:fs = int64(string:v, int64:k) never fails { string:junk = string_concat("qq", "qq"); pass (string_bytes(v)[0i64] => int64) - 90i64 + k; };
func:code = int32(int64:v) never fails { int32:c = 0i32; int64:w = v & 255i64; for (int64:i in 0i64...w) { c = c + 1i32; } pass c; };
